OL,5,CTRADE DEFICIT: STERLING HOLDS UP WELL
OL,6, FFears of mortgage rise recede.108B208
OL,8,CCHEMICAL WEAPONSFSoviets offer
OL,9,F to destroy all stockpiles.....106B206
OL,11,CUDRFplays a necessary role
OL,12,F in Ulster, says Brooke........115B215
OL,13,F
OL,14,CDEAL BOMBINGFAppeal for help...105B205
OL,15,F
OL,16,CTEACHERSFangry at pay proposal.114B214
OL,18,CPOLICEFCall for "British FBI"..103B203
OL,20,CCRIME SQUADFEssex inquiry......110B210
OL,22,T]F This Ceefax page is fromC26-09-89
OL,23,T]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11804
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Fears of an immediate rise in mortgage
OL,6, rates following August's #2 billion
OL,7, trade deficit have receded slightly.
OL,9,FThe pound - the key to interest rates -
OL,10,Fwas briefly thrown off balance by the
OL,11,Ftrade figures, but later recovered.
OL,13,FA BBC correspondent says the Chancellor
OL,14,Fis unlikely to act unless sterling
OL,15,Fcomes under sustained pressure on the
OL,16,Fexchanges.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FBut Mr Lawson has said there can be
OL,19,Fno question of a let-up in the
OL,20,FGovernment's policy of using high
OL,21,Finterest rates to control the economy.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Soviet Union has offered to destroy
OL,6, all chemical weapons if the US will do
OL,7, likewise.
OL,9,FForeign minister Mr Eduard Shevardnadze
OL,10,Fwas replying to a call from President
OL,11,FGeorge Bush for the US and USSR to cut
OL,12,Ftheir stockpiles by 80%.
OL,14,FMr Shevardnadze told the United Nations
OL,15,FGeneral Assembly that Moscow was ready
OL,16,Fto destroy all stockpiles before a
OL,17,Fglobal treaty was signed.
OL,19,FUS Secretary of State Mr James Baker
OL,20,Fdescribed Mr Shevardnadze's speech as
OL,21,F"good, interesting and responsive".
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Moscow's offer to destroy all
OL,6, superpower chemical weapons was a step
OL,7, towards the global elimination of such
OL,8, weapons, said Mr Eduard Shevardnadze.
OL,10,FThe Soviet foreign minister said his
OL,11,Fgovernment was ready to institute
OL,12,Fstrict verification of the destruction
OL,13,Fof these weapons.
OL,15,FHe also said the Soviet Union would
OL,16,Frenounce the use of chemical weapons
OL,17,Funder any circumstances.
OL,19,FThe Soviet Union claims to have 50,000
OL,20,Ftonnes of the weapons; the US is said
OL,21,Fto have 30,000 tonnes.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Ulster Defence Regiment performs a
OL,6, necessary role in Ulster, says Northern
OL,7, Ireland Secretary Mr Peter Brooke.
OL,9,FHe was responding to calls from the
OL,10,FIrish Republic for review of the UDR's
OL,11,Frole following allegations of collusion
OL,12,Fbetween members of the security forces
OL,13,Fand loyalist paramilitiary groups.
OL,15,FBut Mr Brooke said the operation of the
OL,16,FUDR would be discussed at the request
OL,17,Fof the Irish government at the next
OL,18,Fmeeting of the Anglo-Irish conference.
OL,20,FHe said he saw no reason to think the
OL,21,FAnglo-Irish agreement was in jeopardy.
OL,22,       F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, Police investigating the bombing of
OL,6, Deal barracks have appealed for help
OL,7, from garage owners in the south-east.
OL,9,FThey want to hear from any garage who
OL,10,Frepaired a car brought in by one or
OL,11,Fmore Irishmen on September 2.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FPolice believe a car used by the three
OL,14,FIrishmen who rented a house in Deal
OL,15,Fbroke down on that day.
OL,16,F
OL,17,S/FThe inquest into the deaths of 10
OL,18,FRoyal Marines killed by a bomb at
OL,19,Ftheir barracks at Deal in Kent has been
OL,20,Fopened and adjourned until November 14.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Teachers' unions have reacted angrily
OL,6, to the Government's announcement of a
OL,7, 7.5% increase in the cash set aside for
OL,8, teachers' pay next year.
OL,10,FThe Government intends this money to
OL,11,Finclude cash incentives for subjects
OL,12,Fwhere there is a teacher shortage, so
OL,13,Fsome teachers will get less than 7.5%.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FThe National Union of Teachers and the
OL,16,FNational Association of Schoolmasters
OL,17,Fand Union of Women Teachers both spoke
OL,18,Fout against the #600m cash limit.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe NAS/UWT predicted increased demands
OL,21,Ffor militant action.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Home Secretary has called for a
OL,6, national police intelligence unit to
OL,7, be set up to collate information on
OL,8, organised crime and other offences.
OL,10,FMr Douglas Hurd told the police
OL,11,Fsuperintendents' conference in Torquay
OL,12,Fthat the growing sophistication of
OL,13,Fmajor crime necessitated national
OL,14,Fcriminal intelligence.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FThis would operate similarly to the
OL,17,Fexisting Drugs Intelligence Unit using
OL,18,Fa central computer.
OL,20,FSome senior officers see the move as
OL,21,Fa first step towards a British FBI.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11811
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790458424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A top-level police inquiry has been
OL,6, ordered into alleged irregularities in
OL,7, an Essex-based police crime squad.
OL,9,FThe allegations concern the number five
OL,10,Fcrime squad, based in Brentwood, which
OL,11,Fis made up of officers from all over
OL,12,FEast Anglia.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FA spokesman confirmed that an officer
OL,15,Ffrom Essex police has been suspended.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FThe inquiry will be headed by Chief
OL,18,FSuperintendant Peter Nevitt, the head
OL,19,Fof Basildon police, and a report will
OL,20,Fbe sent to the Director of Public
OL,21,FProsecutions.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-09-89   teletextarchive.com
